# Copyrighted arcade ROM dumps -- never commit actual ROM data
*.hex
# Exceptions: these .hex files are NOT rom data, they're self-generated
# synthesis lookup tables the k007420 sprite renderer's own $readmemh calls
# depend on to build at all (ported from Rack 'Em Up, same reasoning as
# that project's own .gitignore) -- must be tracked or a fresh clone won't
# compile.
!rtl/tile_bound1.hex
!rtl/tile_bound2.hex
!rtl/tile_bound3.hex
!rtl/tile_bound4.hex
!rtl/zoom_recip.hex
*.zip
bladestl_roms/
bladestl_extract/
bladestl_extracted/

# Quartus compile logs (regenerated every compile, not meaningful history)
compile_*.log
compile_log*.txt
quartus_compile_log.txt

# Misc local/session artifacts
MiSTer.ini
MiSTer.ini.fetched
NUL
__pycache__/
verilator_bos/roms/
*.ppm
# verilator_bos/filelist.f is a real, hand-written Verilator source-file
# list, not a Quartus-generated artifact -- the broad `*.f` rule above would
# otherwise silently exclude it (essential for anyone to rebuild the harness).
!verilator_bos/filelist.f
verilator_bos/vcd_out/
*.vcd
